1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,500
Imagine putting €10,000 away, and never touching it again.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,450
Thirty years later, at 7% a year,

3
00:00:07,470 --> 00:00:10,174
it's worth about €76,000.

4
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:11,755
You added nothing.

5
00:00:11,775 --> 00:00:12,600
Not one euro.

6
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:13,776
The money did the work.

7
00:00:14,433 --> 00:00:16,158
This is compound interest.

8
00:00:16,178 --> 00:00:18,520
It's often called the eighth wonder of the world.

9
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,105
That quote is usually credited to Einstein.

10
00:00:21,125 --> 00:00:23,130
He almost certainly never said it.

11
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:24,599
But the maths is real.

12
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,389
And here's the part nobody tells you.

13
00:00:28,733 --> 00:00:32,938
Compound interest is slow, then boring, then suddenly unbelievable.

14
00:00:32,958 --> 00:00:35,255
Most people quit during the boring part.

15
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:38,800
Today, I'll explain it so simply it feels illegal.

16
00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:40,180
Seven ideas.

17
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:40,982
No formulas.

18
00:00:41,002 --> 00:00:41,858
Let's begin.

19
00:00:42,967 --> 00:00:43,219
One.

20
00:00:43,239 --> 00:00:44,719
Interest on interest.

21
00:00:45,567 --> 00:00:47,112
Say you have €100,

22
00:00:47,132 --> 00:00:48,867
and it grows 10% a year.

23
00:00:49,167 --> 00:00:51,833
After one year, you have €110.

24
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:55,525
Next year, you don't earn 10% on €100.

25
00:00:55,545 --> 00:00:57,717
You earn it on €110.

26
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:00,662
Your interest starts earning its own interest.

27
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:02,331
It's a snowball.

28
00:01:02,351 --> 00:01:03,785
Small at the top of the hill.

29
00:01:03,805 --> 00:01:04,952
Huge at the bottom.

30
00:01:05,233 --> 00:01:06,873
Same snow, same slope.

31
00:01:06,893 --> 00:01:08,835
The only thing that changed is time.

32
00:01:09,967 --> 00:01:10,197
Two.

33
00:01:10,217 --> 00:01:11,739
The rule of 72.

34
00:01:12,633 --> 00:01:14,793
Want to know how fast your money doubles?

35
00:01:14,813 --> 00:01:17,407
Divide 72 by the yearly return.

36
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:19,230
At 7% a year,

37
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:22,145
72 divided by 7 is about 10.

38
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:24,676
Your money doubles roughly every ten years.

39
00:01:25,433 --> 00:01:30,732
So €10,000 becomes €20,000, then €40,000, then €80,000.

40
00:01:31,133 --> 00:01:32,530
Each doubling is bigger than

41
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:33,724
all the ones before it.

42
00:01:35,033 --> 00:01:35,395
Three.

43
00:01:35,415 --> 00:01:36,546
Time beats money.

44
00:01:37,467 --> 00:01:38,747
Meet Anna and Ben.

45
00:01:38,767 --> 00:01:42,214
Both invest €200 a month, at 7% a year.

46
00:01:42,667 --> 00:01:44,302
Anna starts at 25.

47
00:01:44,322 --> 00:01:46,017
Ben starts at 35.

48
00:01:46,037 --> 00:01:47,561
Both stop at 65.

49
00:01:48,267 --> 00:01:50,772
Ben puts in €72,000.

50
00:01:50,792 --> 00:01:54,075
He ends with about €244,000.

51
00:01:54,533 --> 00:01:57,268
Anna puts in only €24,000 more.

52
00:01:57,288 --> 00:02:00,936
She ends with about €525,000.

53
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:04,075
Ten extra years more than doubled her money.

54
00:02:04,095 --> 00:02:06,195
Starting early beats starting big.

55
00:02:07,333 --> 00:02:07,638
Four.

56
00:02:07,658 --> 00:02:08,813
The boring years.

57
00:02:09,767 --> 00:02:11,622
Here's why most people give up.

58
00:02:11,642 --> 00:02:14,062
After ten years of €200 a month,

59
00:02:14,082 --> 00:02:16,635
Anna has about €35,000.

60
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,080
Only about €11,000 of that is growth.

61
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,961
It feels like nothing is happening.

62
00:02:22,733 --> 00:02:24,083
But around year 11,

63
00:02:24,103 --> 00:02:25,737
the growth in a single year becomes

64
00:02:25,757 --> 00:02:28,113
bigger than everything she puts in that year.

65
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:30,355
After that, the curve bends upward.

66
00:02:30,375 --> 00:02:32,358
The boring part was the foundation.

67
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:33,883
Five.

68
00:02:33,903 --> 00:02:35,467
It works against you too.

69
00:02:36,467 --> 00:02:38,985
Compound interest doesn't care which side you're on.

70
00:02:39,367 --> 00:02:40,821
Some credit cards and store

71
00:02:40,841 --> 00:02:43,155
credit charge around 20% a year.

72
00:02:43,967 --> 00:02:45,762
At 20%, a debt doubles

73
00:02:45,782 --> 00:02:47,202
in less than four years.

74
00:02:47,222 --> 00:02:50,012
That's the rule of 72, working for the bank.

75
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:53,145
So before you invest, pay off expensive debt.

76
00:02:53,165 --> 00:02:55,155
It's the best return you'll ever get.

77
00:02:56,233 --> 00:02:56,510
Six.

78
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:57,912
Fees compound too.

79
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:01,675
A fee of 1.8% a year sounds tiny.

80
00:03:01,695 --> 00:03:02,546
It isn't.

81
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,535
€200 a month for 30 years:

82
00:03:05,555 --> 00:03:11,040
with fees of 0.2%, about €235,000.

83
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:15,319
With 1.8%, about €173,000.

84
00:03:16,133 --> 00:03:17,138
Same money in.

85
00:03:17,158 --> 00:03:19,468
Over €60,000 less out.

86
00:03:19,488 --> 00:03:22,056
The fee compounds against you, every single year.

87
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:23,680
Seven.

88
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:25,947
Inflation is compounding in reverse.

89
00:03:26,767 --> 00:03:28,732
Prices rise a little every year.

90
00:03:28,752 --> 00:03:31,427
The European Central Bank aims for 2%.

91
00:03:31,833 --> 00:03:33,368
At 2% inflation,

92
00:03:33,388 --> 00:03:35,348
money sitting in cash loses almost

93
00:03:35,368 --> 00:03:37,657
half its buying power in 30 years.

94
00:03:38,367 --> 00:03:41,452
That's why long-term money usually can't just sit still.

95
00:03:41,472 --> 00:03:47,982
Over the last 125 years, global stocks grew about 5% a year faster than inflation,

96
00:03:48,002 --> 00:03:48,737
on average.

97
00:03:49,067 --> 00:03:49,957
Not every year.

98
00:03:49,977 --> 00:03:51,377
Some years were terrible.

99
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:53,866
But over decades, time did the heavy lifting.

100
00:03:55,067 --> 00:03:56,246
Final message.

101
00:03:57,333 --> 00:03:59,198
Compound interest isn't magic.

102
00:03:59,218 --> 00:04:01,463
It's just patience, written in maths.

103
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:03,020
Start early.

104
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:04,203
Start small if you have to.

105
00:04:04,223 --> 00:04:05,283
Keep fees low.

106
00:04:05,303 --> 00:04:06,684
Kill expensive debt.

107
00:04:07,433 --> 00:04:08,838
And then, the hardest part:

108
00:04:08,858 --> 00:04:10,657
do nothing, for a very long time.

109
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:14,160
This is education, not financial advice.

110
00:04:14,180 --> 00:04:16,865
The numbers here are examples, not promises.

111
00:04:16,885 --> 00:04:18,585
If this helped, subscribe.

112
00:04:18,605 --> 00:04:18,835
Next up:

113
00:04:18,855 --> 00:04:21,946
how to save money so easily it feels illegal.
